  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the Haut-Var, the Bresque river drops 44 metres from cliffs of pink tufa and travertine, dotted with pines, fig trees and cushions of moss, into a turquoise pool. A path runs through the forest to a viewing balcony above the pool. The Dracénie Provence Verdon tourist office calls it the prettiest waterfall in the Haut Var, and the Verdon regional park classes the site as a "heart of nature".</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access to the pool beneath the waterfall and swimming there are banned because of falling rocks: the tufa cliffs are very fragile and crumbly. So this isn't a place to cool off with your dog, only a site to admire from the viewpoint. The tourist office says dogs must be kept on a leash and must not leave the marked routes (sensitive natural area, Natura 2000), and recommends good shoes. The park's sheet adds that the steps are slippery in the rain.</p>
      <p>The viewpoint is on Place du 8 mai 1945, in the village, about 15 minutes' walk away; the Verdon park recommends the ramparts car park. The way down is by several flights of steps and through woodland, and you return the same way: the climb back can be tiring in hot weather, so bring water for your dog. In 2026, according to the tourist office, the right bank stayed closed throughout the summer season, and the Var wildfire-risk map can restrict access to wooded areas in summer.</p>
      <p>Parking is paid and compulsory from 1 April to 30 September, 9am-7pm: 30 minutes free, then €1 every 15 minutes. Access to the viewpoint itself is free.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come early or late in the day in summer, when the site is quieter and the steps are cooler for your dog's paws.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old village of Sillans, with its medieval ramparts, its parish church of Saint-Étienne and its château, can be explored on foot before or after the walk. Lac de Sainte-Croix, south of the Verdon, lets you extend the day by the water. For information, the Dracénie Provence Verdon tourist office can be reached on +33 4 94 60 34 90.</p>
    </div>

